    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.completion\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nI used to use vim-mucomplete, and I really liked the way it automagically handled fallbacks. Basically, in 99% cases I want to use  LSP completion / omnicompletion or file path completion. File paths almost always begins with a `/`, `.`, or `\\` symbol, which is unusual in programming language syntax. \r\n\r\ntl;dr I think mini.completions should fallback to file completion when a `.` or `/` symbol is under the cursor. ",
    "closed_at": "2023-04-22T14:37:09Z",
