        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "If you think it's too much of a check to add to mini, I can add it myself in config. Just seems a shame to burn my fallback for the occasional path. What I really liked about mucomplete is the fallback chaining. Maybe I will implement that as a custom fallback function. In nearly all cases what I want to complete is LSP if exists, else omnifunc if exists, else word in buffer if exists, else dictionary if exists, else path if exists. So I think a plugin that \"does the right thing\" would be useful to avoid huge configs for no reason. ",
